WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.572 --> 00:00:14.175
"Are you ready for battle, my boys?"

2
00:00:14.996 --> 00:00:17.176
shouted Peter with great excitement.

3
00:00:18.457 --> 00:00:24.018
From various parts of the lagoon, the boys answered, "Ay, ay!

4
00:00:24.258 --> 00:00:25.979
We'll get those pirates!"

5
00:00:27.779 --> 00:00:29.280
And the battle was on.

6
00:00:30.464 --> 00:00:36.468
The boys fought bravely against Smee and Starkey, forcing them out of their boat and into the water.

7
00:00:37.589 --> 00:00:39.070
Heads bobbed up and down.

8
00:00:40.371 --> 00:00:41.372
It was a close fight.

9
00:00:42.553 --> 00:00:47.176
At last, the boys captured the boat, and the two pirates swam away.

10
00:00:48.737 --> 00:00:54.041
Fearless as they were, none of the boys wanted to fight Captain Hook, who was in the water

11
00:00:54.121 --> 00:01:00.721
too. They had promised Peter that Captain Hook would be his, but they also trembled at the thought

12
00:01:00.761 --> 00:01:02.041
of Hook's iron claw.

13
00:01:03.121 --> 00:01:09.443
It was at this battle, on Marooners' Rock, that Peter and Hook would finally meet face-to-face!

14
00:01:10.963 --> 00:01:13.424
Hook pulled himself up on the rock to take a breath.

15
00:01:14.524 --> 00:01:16.265
Peter climbed up the other side.

16
00:01:17.225 --> 00:01:22.306
Because the rock was slippery, they had to crawl on their knees, keeping their heads down.

17
00:01:23.287 --> 00:01:24.887
Neither knew the other was coming.

18
00:01:25.747 --> 00:01:30.285
As they both reached for a grip on the slippery rock, their hands suddenly touched.

19
00:01:31.746 --> 00:01:35.728
Their heads popped up, and Hook and Peter were nose to nose.

20
00:01:36.849 --> 00:01:39.810
Quickly, Peter grabbed the knife from Hook's belt.

21
00:01:40.931 --> 00:01:45.433
But before he struck his foe, Peter noticed that he was on the highest part of the rock.

22
00:01:46.594 --> 00:01:47.915
It seemed very unfair.

23
00:01:49.556 --> 00:01:55.559
So instead of stabbing Hook right away, Peter extended his hand to help Hook up so they would

24
00:01:55.639 --> 00:01:57.140
both be on equal footing.

25
00:01:58.240 --> 00:02:01.463
But rather than taking Peter's hand, Hook bit it.

26
00:02:02.444 --> 00:02:05.006
Outraged, Peter stood motionless.

27
00:02:05.526 --> 00:02:06.327
He was in shock.

28
00:02:07.588 --> 00:02:10.210
People remember the first time life is unfair to them.

29
00:02:11.291 --> 00:02:15.494
Though they may forgive the unfairness, they are never quite the same after.

30
00:02:16.615 --> 00:02:17.496
But not Peter.

31
00:02:18.036 --> 00:02:21.599
He had met unfairness before, but he always forgot.

32
00:02:22.680 --> 00:02:27.164
Perhaps this was the real difference between Peter and other boys who grow older.

33
00:02:28.416 --> 00:02:32.999
While Peter stood there stunned, Hook's iron hand clawed him several times.

34
00:02:33.740 --> 00:02:35.681
Peter was badly wounded.

35
00:02:36.522 --> 00:02:40.124
During the battle, the Lost Boys lost track of Wendy and Peter.

36
00:02:41.205 --> 00:02:45.728
After a while they saw Hook in the water swimming away as fast as he could.

37
00:02:47.269 --> 00:02:51.052
Behind him was the crocodile in pursuit of his favorite food.

38
00:02:52.072 --> 00:02:54.614
The boys decided to make their way back home.

39
00:02:55.955 --> 00:03:01.104
Occasionally they shouted "Peter!

40
00:03:01.124 --> 00:03:02.505
Wendy!" but they expected no answer.

41
00:03:03.666 --> 00:03:07.188
They were sure that Peter and Wendy had already made it back home.

42
00:03:08.729 --> 00:03:13.593
Left behind, Wendy had swum around the lagoon on her own and was now worn-out.

43
00:03:14.754 --> 00:03:18.756
With his last bit of strength, Peter pulled her up onto Marooners' Rock.

44
00:03:19.617 --> 00:03:24.020
They both lay there, tired and weak and unable to speak.

45
00:03:25.041 --> 00:03:26.301
The tide was coming in.

46
00:03:27.382 --> 00:03:31.309
Finally Peter said, "Look, the water is rising."

47
00:03:32.851 --> 00:03:36.194
Wendy did not understand, so Peter tried to explain.

48
00:03:36.214 --> 00:03:41.018
"You're too weak to swim or fly home, and I am badly wounded.

49
00:03:42.259 --> 00:03:44.181
Soon the water will cover this rock."

50
00:03:44.201 --> 00:03:47.563
"You mean we are going to drown?"

51
00:03:48.184 --> 00:03:49.465
she asked weakly.

52
00:03:50.406 --> 00:03:53.969
"Unless we find a way to leave this rock," he answered.

53
00:03:55.651 --> 00:04:00.938
As they clung to each other, Peter searched the water for something that might keep them afloat.

54
00:04:01.839 --> 00:04:03.440
Floating by was Starkey's hat.

55
00:04:04.461 --> 00:04:05.962
Quickly, Peter grabbed it.

56
00:04:06.422 --> 00:04:08.483
But it was too small to be of much help.

57
00:04:09.484 --> 00:04:11.726
Nevertheless, he placed it on his head.

58
00:04:13.107 --> 00:04:16.529
Then suddenly something very light brushed against Peter.

59
00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:20.452
It was the tail of a kite that was flying high above.

60
00:04:21.472 --> 00:04:24.875
Michael had made it some days ago, and it had blown away.

61
00:04:26.748 --> 00:04:27.949
"Look it's Michael's kite!"

62
00:04:28.529 --> 00:04:29.110
said Peter.

63
00:04:29.130 --> 00:04:31.851
"It might be able to carry you home."

64
00:04:32.492 --> 00:04:33.573
Peter grabbed hold of it.

65
00:04:34.773 --> 00:04:38.296
With new energy, he tied the string of the kite around Wendy's waist.

66
00:04:38.316 --> 00:04:40.217
"What about you?"

67
00:04:40.978 --> 00:04:41.578
asked Wendy.

68
00:04:41.598 --> 00:04:44.480
"You must tie it around yourself too."

69
00:04:44.500 --> 00:04:47.282
"This kite isn't big enough.

70
00:04:47.742 --> 00:04:51.044
It will only lift one person," replied Peter.

71
00:04:51.064 --> 00:04:55.027
"I won't go without you," said Wendy.

72
00:04:56.236 --> 00:05:00.303
But, with his last bit of strength, Peter had already pushed her from the rock.

73
00:05:01.385 --> 00:05:04.871
In seconds, she was in the air and almost out of sight.
